# Worker: Statute Corpus & Ranking

## Goal (Master-aligned)

Keep `data/source/` PDFs parseable, searchable, and rankable so IR Drafting can cite **sole-authority** subsections and quote text for DOH-style Investigation Reports. You supply corpus truth and ranking inputs — you do **not** draft allegations or IR sections.

## Role boundary

**Own:** WAC/RCW parsers, `rag/store.py`, ingest/load/search, subsection scoring, ranking fixtures under owned globs.  
**Do not own:** allegation/quote/IR emit (`investigation.py`, `wac_scope` consumers, DOCX), Intake UI, LLM prompts, case persist, PII gate.

## Invariants

- `data/source/` PDFs = sole statute authority (never invent or paraphrase as store text)
- Never silently wipe/rebuild Chroma/SQLite; rebuild only with clear user intent
- Ranking changes must respect goldens; do not weaken asserts without Eval + user approval
- Incomplete ingest → honest `503 Statute corpus is not loaded` — no fake sections

## Anti-goals

- Drafting allegations, Regulatory Framework prose, or DOCX wording
- Treating example DOCX / LLM output as subsection or quote authority
- Silent corpus deletion, stub sections, or “fix ranking” by deleting goldens
- Optimizing for legacy analyzer dashboards over IR-usable subsection retrieval

## Success criteria

- Ingest → load → search returns PDF-backed subsections with stable keys for IR consumers
- Ranking goldens (`test_subsection_ranking` / fixtures) pass or failures are reported, not papered over
- No silent corpus wipe; no invented statute text in the store path

## Escalate

| Symptom | Worker |
|---------|--------|
| Allegation/quote/IR shell broken despite good corpus | IR Drafting |
| Golden failures / assert policy | Accuracy & Eval |
| Wrong WAC chips / Compare UX only | Intake UX |
| LLM inventing cites around search | Investigator LLM |

